<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-cefa1.3 — schema type-hygiene pass, Tier A + Tier B, P2 (epic
    nexus-cefa1; plan of record T2 nexus/plan-schema-type-hygiene-2026-08-12
    [22360]). Template: catalog-031-type-hygiene.xml (nexus-cefa1.2, P1).

    Retires two RDR-152 SQLite-port columns on nexus.hook_failures to their
    real Postgres types, in ONE ALTER TABLE (one table-rewrite pass covering
    both columns, not two separate rewrites) — mirroring catalog-031-1's
    one-ALTER-for-three-cols shape:

    - is_batch (Tier A): INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 -> boolean NOT NULL
      DEFAULT false, via DROP DEFAULT -> TYPE boolean USING (is_batch <> 0)
      -> SET DEFAULT false. NOT NULL is preserved automatically across
      ALTER COLUMN TYPE (never touched); only DEFAULT is dropped and re-set
      because a numeric DEFAULT 0 is not valid input for a boolean column.
      Same shape as catalog-031-3's legacy_grandfathered.
    - batch_doc_ids (Tier B): nullable TEXT, no default -> jsonb NULL, via
      TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(batch_doc_ids, '')::jsonb. No DROP
      DEFAULT/DROP NOT NULL needed — telemetry-001-baseline.xml:240 ships
      this column as plain `batch_doc_ids TEXT,` with neither.

    ALTER COLUMN TYPE is ordinary DDL (an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table rewrite),
    not RLS-filtered DML — no FORCE RLS toggle needed for this changeset,
    and it does not touch a row via INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.

    Data-safety evidence: T2 nexus/schema-hygiene-p0-preflight-2026-08-15
    [22588] (nexus-cefa1.1). Cloud (the only populated deployment; this
    box's local substrate is a fresh hermetic pytest engine with no seeded
    data): hook_failures.batch_doc_ids total_rows=247, null_count=247,
    empty_string_count=0, invalid_cast_count=0 — every row is already NULL,
    none are '' or malformed, so the NULLIF(...,'')::jsonb USING clause
    above has nothing to convert and is confirmed safe. is_batch was NOT
    part of the P0 probe (it is Tier A boolean, not Tier B jsonb) — its live
    value domain was instead verified by reading the writer: every INSERT
    that sets is_batch goes through TelemetryRepository.recordHookFailure,
    .importHookFailureRow, or .importHookFailuresBatch, and all three write
    `isBatch ? 1 : 0` (or the batch path's `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...) ? 1 :
    0`) — the column's value domain is mechanically {0, 1}, never any other
    integer, so `USING (is_batch <> 0)` is exhaustive and safe by
    construction, independent of any live-data probe.

    Consumer audit (nexus-cefa1.3, mirroring nexus-cefa1.2's sweep): the
    wire is ALREADY boolean end to end for is_batch (TelemetryHandler.java
    handleHookFailureRecord ~352 reads `Boolean.TRUE.equals(body.get(
    "is_batch"))`; handleImport's hook_failures case ~504 the same;
    TelemetryRepository.getHookFailures ~487 already emits a JSON boolean)
    — this changeset does not change that wire shape, only the storage
    column's own type, retiring the `isBatch ? 1 : 0` / `!= 0` integer
    shims in TelemetryRepository. batch_doc_ids is, and remains, a raw JSON
    string on the wire (a caller-supplied JSON-encoded array, e.g.
    hook_registry.py's `json.dumps(doc_ids)`; taxonomy_cmd.py's status
    command defensively `json.loads`s it back with a try/except fallback,
    confirming JSON was always the intended shape of this "TEXT" column).
    Two test call sites — TelemetryRepositoryTest.java
    (hookFailures_read_returnsRowsAndExactAggregates) and Python's
    tests/db/test_onjvy_read_routes.py
    (test_hook_failure_batch_variant_carries_its_doc_ids) — wrote a
    non-JSON opaque string ("d1,d2") through this field to exercise it as a
    generic opaque-string column; that was always incidental to TEXT typing
    and not a real production shape (no production writer ever emits
    anything but a JSON array), so both are updated to a valid JSON array
    in the corresponding bead's Java/Python changes rather than carried
    forward as a genuine consumer needing a compatibility shim.

    ANALYZE after the rewrite (BUG-0148 invariant, rdr180-16-analyze-
    rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically enforced by
    tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py) — the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE above
    resets nexus.hook_failures's planner statistics.

    Rollback: is_batch mirrors catalog-031-3's legacy_grandfathered exactly
    — TYPE INTEGER USING (CASE WHEN is_batch THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), DEFAULT 0
    restored. batch_doc_ids mirrors catalog-031-2's created_at (nullable,
    no default TEXT column) rather than the NOT-NULL-DEFAULT-'' columns in
    catalog-031-1: TYPE TEXT USING batch_doc_ids::text, which casts a jsonb
    NULL back to a TEXT NULL for free (no COALESCE-to-'' needed, since the
    pre-migration column never had a NOT NULL/DEFAULT '' to restore in the
    first place — telemetry-001-baseline.xml:240 confirms this precisely).

    Ordering: registered after catalog-031-type-hygiene.xml and before
    grants-nexus-svc.xml, NOT back in the telemetry-00N family's own
    section near the top of the changelog. This matches the master
    changelog's actual, established convention for every new changeset
    since RDR-156 (catalog-002 through catalog-031, taxonomy-002 through
    -007, aspects-002, etc. all append near the current tail rather than
    splicing back into their family's original block) — see
    db.changelog-master.xml's own header comment on the catalog-031
    <include> for the identical reasoning applied to that file.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset telemetry-004-1-hook-failures-type-hygiene ───────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="telemetry-004-1-hook-failures-type-hygiene" author="nexus-cefa1.3">
        <comment>
            hook_failures.is_batch INTEGER -> boolean; hook_failures.batch_doc_ids TEXT -> jsonb
            NULL (ONE ALTER TABLE, one rewrite).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.hook_failures
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch TYPE boolean USING (is_batch &lt;&gt; 0),
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch SET DEFAULT false,
    ALTER COLUMN batch_doc_ids TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(batch_doc_ids, '')::jsonb;

-- BUG-0148 invariant (rdr180-16-analyze-rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically
-- enforced by tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py): the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE
-- above rewrites hook_failures and resets its planner statistics — ANALYZE it in
-- the same pass so a stale-stats plan flip cannot silently degrade the
-- `nx doctor` hook-failures read path.
ANALYZE nexus.hook_failures;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.hook_failures
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch TYPE INTEGER USING (CASE WHEN is_batch THEN 1 ELSE 0 END),
    ALTER COLUMN is_batch SET DEFAULT 0,
    ALTER COLUMN batch_doc_ids TYPE TEXT USING batch_doc_ids::text;

ANALYZE nexus.hook_failures;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
